codex
The pinned Lean binary is present, but its runtime cannot resolve its own executable path inside this container, so plain `lake build` currently fails before elaboration. I’ve isolated that to Lean’s `uv_exepath` startup call and am applying a local `/tmp` runtime shim that only supplies the already-pinned executable path; it does not alter the project, Base, theorem, or toolchain contents.
apply patch
patch: completed
/tmp/lean_app_path.c
diff --git a//tmp/lean_app_path.c b//tmp/lean_app_path.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..845c68764e6f1a6535ad9ccb85b4d26b62aad525
--- /dev/null
+++ b//tmp/lean_app_path.c
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+int uv_exepath(char *buffer, size_t *size) {
+  static const char path[] =
+      "/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/bin/lean";
+  const size_t length = sizeof(path) - 1;
+  if (*size <= length) {
+    *size = length + 1;
+    return -105;
+  }
+  memcpy(buffer, path, length + 1);
+  *size = length;
+  return 0;
+}
